{{/*
  beads/load-context — the standard 4-command "load everything you need to
  reason about a specific bead" block: full detail, dependency tree, existing
  children, prior comments. Used by prompts that operate on a single target
  bead (assess, discuss, investigate, and future consumers).

  The template argument (`.` inside the fragment) is the target bead ID as a
  plain string. Callers typically resolve it into a local `$target` variable
  first, then pass it through:

      {{ $target := "" -}}
      {{ if .Session.BeadsIssue }}{{ $target = .Session.BeadsIssue }}
      {{ else if .Args.IssueID }}{{ $target = .Args.IssueID }}{{ end -}}

      {{ if $target -}}
      ## Step 1 — Load the bead and its context

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/load-context" $target }}

      Read everything carefully. <prompt-specific reader guidance here>.
      {{- end }}

  Passing the string directly (rather than wrapping in a struct/dict) keeps
  callers terse and avoids depending on template helpers the project's
  FuncMap does not expose.
*/}}
```bash
bd show {{ . }} --long --json     # description, acceptance, design, notes, labels, status
bd dep tree {{ . }}               # blockers and what it blocks
bd show {{ . }} --children --json # existing child beads (if any)
bd comments {{ . }}               # prior discussion, if any
```
